  "description": "Generalized nullable value representation.",
  "id": "NCoreUtils.Maybe",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-12T13:16:00.61Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "COaFtb43akGU/RCdFLU17k51aEn3WSedi0zHB//SGrEgh02wjltnegEY6CWV3HrD6yDpP0cYjT5pImGHusAzGA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 133690,
  "published": "2026-10-12T13:12:00.1Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes:\n- Aggregate, ToEnumerable, ToList and ToArray returned the opposite result (value for empty, nothing for non-empty).\n- MaybeMax returned the minimum for HashSet and general IEnumerable sources.\n- Enumerators of general IEnumerable sources were not disposed.\n- As<TDerived>() turned Just(null) into an empty value; it now returns Just(null) if TDerived can hold null.\nChanges:\n- GetOrDefault() returns T? while GetOrDefault(defaultValue) returns T (no longer nullable).\n- ToString() returns an empty string instead of null.\n- GetHashCode of Maybe and MinMax distinguishes empty, Just(null) and common values (e.g. Just(0)).\n- Pick throws an exception with a descriptive message if no value was picked.\n- Equals(other, comparer) accepts a null comparer (uses the default comparer).\n- MinMax supports deconstruction (Deconstruct); Destruct is obsolete.\n- net461: System.Memory is no longer a dependency.\nAnalyzers (NCoreUtils.Maybe.Analyzers, referenced automatically):\n- NCMAYBE001: As<T>() with a non-nullable target on a nullable source, with code fix.\n- NCMAYBE002: null literal converted to Maybe<T> (results in an empty value), with code fix.",
